knext bundled fix for vinext 1.1.0 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3741
What it fixes: In a Nitro production build `/_next/image` never reached vinext's image handler: the App Router handler answered it with a 302 to the source asset, so the response a client sees came from Nitro's static handler and carried no Next.js image headers.
When Nitro's app is on globalThis.__nitro__.default the handler now serves the image itself
through handleNitroImageOptimization, which follows Next.js: the source request carries no
client headers, only Content-Type/Content-Length/ETag/Last-Modified/Cache-Control are kept from
the source (never Set-Cookie), non-image sources are rejected, and Cache-Control is
`public, max-age=<max(source max-age, 14400)>, must-revalidate` (immutable only for hashed
/_next/static/media sources). Dev keeps the redirect. The `x-nextjs-cache: MISS` header comes
from the vinext-3734 patch, which this one applies after.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3741. Note: upstream #3741 differs from this port (it reads `images.minimumCacheTTL` from config and wires Nitro via a build-time `resolveImageSourceFetch` option); this patch keeps the behaviour knext shipped. Re-port to the final #3741 once it merges or is released.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

